<title>FRANCE: Printemps main store reopens after strike.</title>
<headline>Printemps main store reopens after strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The flagship Printemps department store in Paris reopened for business on Thursday after being closed for a day and a half by a maintenance workers' strike.</p>
<p>&quot;It was open at lunch,&quot; a spokeswoman for retail conglomerate Pinault-Printemps-Redoute said.</p>
<p>She said the strike had finished and the management was in discussions with the maintenance workers' representatives.</p>
<p>Printemps has 17 stores in France and around a dozen abroad.</p>
</text>
